1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
A hundred dollars a day can beat a million. Sometimes.

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:07,440
Here's the choice. One million dollars, cash, today.

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:11,500
Or a hundred dollars every single day, for the rest of your life.

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,020
No taxes, no interest, just those two piles of money.

5
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,900
Most people grab the million, because it's a million.

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,080
Hit like if you'd grab it without thinking.

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,580
But a hundred a day is about three thousand dollars a month.

8
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,600
That's basically your rent and groceries, covered forever.

9
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,340
After one year, that's thirty-six thousand five hundred dollars.

10
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,800
So when does it catch the million? On day ten thousand.

11
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:36,180
That's about twenty-seven years of checks.

12
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:39,040
Send this to the friend who'd blow the million in a month.

13
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,840
And it keeps going. So the real question is your age.

14
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:46,760
Start at twenty-five and live to eighty, and you collect about two million.

15
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,240
That's double the million, just for waking up.

16
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:51,980
Start at forty, and you still win by eighty.

17
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,480
Follow if you're doing your own age math right now.

18
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,160
But start at sixty, and by eighty you've only got seven hundred thirty thousand dollars.

19
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:03,220
Now the boring million wins, by two hundred seventy thousand dollars.

20
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,940
So the daily money only wins after twenty-seven years.

21
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,600
Million or a hundred a day? One word.

